    "exact_sme54_block": "### SME-54 — BH independent FDR\n**Pages:** benjamini-hochberg-independent-fdr-control / benjamini-hochberg-independent-fdr-control-examples. **A:** For $q\\in(0,1)$, $m$ mutually independent p-values, exactly uniform continuous true-null p-values and arbitrary false-null laws, define $R=\\max\\{k:p_{(k)}\\le kq/m\\}$, with $R=0$ if the set is empty, and reject ranks $1,\\ldots,R$. Prove $\\mathrm{FDR}=E[V/(R\\vee1)]\\le(m_0/m)q$ by the source leave-one-out/induction lemma conditioning on false-null values. This is FDR control, not FWER control. Discrete superuniform true-null extensions require an additional proof and are not included. **B:** small independent family/FDR-FWER. **Requires:** SME-52; MSF-08; published mutual-independence/product-law supplier. **Sources:** BH95 Thm.1 p.6/Appendix A pp.12–13; BY01 pp.16–17.\n",
    "block_raw_sha256": "8c09cbb48e78d3e03fa786f4ef596a82cd94ec6dcbdddfbd3a42ffe50443b419",
    "actual_main_clause": "Requires SME52 page, MSF08 and published independence/product-law supplier; main paragraph does not itself list an exact canonical direct item ID. Native final reviewer reports direct-ID designs; owner may explicitly approve this mathematically equivalent substitution without changing scope.",
    "optional_exact_clause_for_root_only": "**Interface clarification:** SME-52 supplies the prespecified finite-family and parameterwise null-valid/FDP/FDR/FWER interface. The local [[def-false-discovery-rate-and-familywise-error-rate]] is an approved fixed-law specialization of [[def-null-valid-p-value-and-fwer-fdr]]: for each $\\theta$, put $P=P_\\theta$, $I_0=I_0(\\theta)$, and $D_i=\\{x:i\\in\\mathcal R(x)\\}$. Theorem/example may use that equivalent local definition directly; the SME-52 page prerequisite is retained. No canonical direct item dependency is required solely for its ID when the current proof actually uses this complete local specialization.",
    "write_performed": false
  },
